WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.045
It was a normal day for Leo.

00:00:02.045 --> 00:00:04.096
His shop was ready, but customers kept

00:00:04.096 --> 00:00:04.994
walking.

00:00:04.994 --> 00:00:06.917
For days, he faced one question: who

00:00:06.917 --> 00:00:08.776
should he reach, and what should he

00:00:08.776 --> 00:00:09.545
offer?

00:00:09.683 --> 00:00:11.558
Could AI do this for Leo?

00:00:12.158 --> 00:00:15.058
Meet Market Metro, a simulated commerce world

00:00:15.108 --> 00:00:18.658
where AI agents analyze behavior, train models,

00:00:18.708 --> 00:00:20.958
test campaigns and measure what works.

00:00:21.083 --> 00:00:23.408
The ontology gives data meaning.

00:00:23.483 --> 00:00:26.258
It connects shoppers, products and payments, and

00:00:26.333 --> 00:00:28.383
shows the agent which history and signals

00:00:28.433 --> 00:00:29.458
it can trust.

00:00:29.583 --> 00:00:32.258
The agent spots the opportunity, chooses twenty

00:00:32.283 --> 00:00:34.108
eight days of history, and trains two

00:00:34.158 --> 00:00:35.033
models.

00:00:35.108 --> 00:00:37.183
Every decision leaves a checkpoint.

00:00:37.317 --> 00:00:40.196
Before anything launches, the verifier tests both

00:00:40.196 --> 00:00:42.605
models in matching markets and selects the

00:00:42.605 --> 00:00:45.417
stronger result for merchants and PayPal.

00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:47.900
Then it happens: a shopper returns.

00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:49.850
They buy the ninety six dollar table,

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:51.575
and it arrives the next day.

00:00:51.625 --> 00:00:53.775
The same request went unfilled under fixed

00:00:53.825 --> 00:00:54.575
rules.

00:00:54.717 --> 00:00:57.253
PayPal Sandbox captures that exact order and

00:00:57.253 --> 00:00:59.921
sends the receipt back to the warehouse.

00:00:59.921 --> 00:01:02.324
The payment, fee and merchant proceeds all

00:01:02.324 --> 00:01:04.392
connect to the same purchase.

00:01:04.517 --> 00:01:07.570
The same market delivers sixteen more purchases

00:01:07.570 --> 00:01:10.623
kept, extra payment volume, and higher merchant

00:01:10.623 --> 00:01:13.676
contribution and modeled PayPal net, even after

00:01:13.676 --> 00:01:14.644
AI cost.

00:01:14.644 --> 00:01:17.101
Every gain is measured against the same

00:01:17.101 --> 00:01:18.367
fixed rules.

00:01:18.517 --> 00:01:20.442
A G Grid makes the entire journey

00:01:20.492 --> 00:01:23.792
inspectable: the models, the agent's decisions, the

00:01:23.842 --> 00:01:25.642
payments, and the results.

00:01:25.717 --> 00:01:28.017
Open any step and see the evidence.

00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:29.225
Market Metro.

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:31.505
Agentic commerce that learns, and shows its

00:01:31.555 --> 00:01:32.180
work.
